.el .ds Aq '
.TH ox-export 1  "ox-export " 
.SH NAME
ox\-export \- Export cached outputs for adoption, or translate an Oxymakefile
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBox\-export\fR [\fB\-\-manifest\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fITARGETS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export cached outputs for adoption, or translate an Oxymakefile
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write a versioned output\-adoption manifest to this path
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR [default: Oxymakefile.toml]
Path to the Oxymakefile to export (default: Oxymakefile.toml)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Write output to a file instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fITARGETS\fR]
Targets to export, or the legacy translation format (snakemake/wdl)
